      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:2j5h6g'
    '|a||And it keeps moving. In 2023, seventy-two percent of Americans told Pew that tipping is expected in more places than five years before.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1euvovg'
    '|b||Here''s my objection. Jon Elster argued that norms aren''t tools for an outcome; they''re held up by shame and guilt. Put guilt into a cost curve and you''ve included the norm, not explained it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:fsw18l'
    '|a||Ofer Azar adds a puzzle: if people tipped only to dodge disapproval, the norm should slowly erode. Instead American tips have crept up.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1lvji5r'
    '|b||So tipping must also pay in something else: looking generous, or feeling generous.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1dk9y9k'
    '|a||How sure are we? That a norm can hold itself up through what people expect of each other: mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1dp4rlx'
    '|b||That guilt is the glue: contested. When researchers told people exactly what the other side expected, the link largely disappeared.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1lzipby'
    '|a||And where norms come from, and why they shift: still open.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:15xvu85'
    '|a||Three new cases. Mia''s bakery in Harbourtown adds a card screen suggesting 10, 15 or 20 percent. In the expectation model, why might people who never tipped for bread start?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1hjs8ja'
    '|a||The screen announces that a tip is now expected. Once you think someone expects one, leaving nothing starts to sting.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||In 2015 Danny Meyer dropped tipping at his New York restaurants and raised menu prices by about a fifth. What does the norm model warn about going it alone?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||His menus look dearer. Every rival''s price still leaves the tip out, so one restaurant can''t leave the norm alone without looking expensive.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Food-delivery apps arrived with no tipping custom of their own. In the expectation model, what sets the tip there?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7800
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Whatever the default makes people expect: the suggested tip tells you what the courier expects, and falling short of it stings.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So why tip a waiter you''ll never see again? Because a norm says so, and keeping it feels better than breaking it, whether that''s guilt, pride or habit. Economics can show why a norm holds; which number a country lands on is its history.':
